    <string id="str_culture_description.crusader" text="{=crusaderdescription}German culture in the 13th century, within the Northern Crusades context, was marked by the fusion of religious zealotry with the ideals of Ritterschaft (knighthood), embodied by the nobility who combined Christian piety with martial prowess while embracing the chivalric code and Minnesang traditions in their courts. The period saw German military and religious customs, architecture, and urban organization being exported to the Baltic territories through the Teutonic Order, whose members - often drawn from the ministeriales class - created a distinct cultural synthesis of monastic discipline and warrior ethos." />
