    <string id="str_culture_description.curonian_raiders" text="{=curonian_raidersdescription}Curonian culture of the 13th century represented the seafaring Baltic tribes (Kurši). Known as fierce warriors, traders, and raiders along the Baltic Sea, they combined maritime traditions with pagan religious practices and strong clan-based social structures. Their settlements included coastal hillforts, wooden homesteads, and sacred groves where rituals were performed." />
