    <!--<string id="str_neutral_term_for_culture.oeselian_raiders" text="{=oeselian_raiders}oeselian_raiders" />-->
    <string id="str_culture_description.oeselian_raiders" text="{=oeselian_raidersdescription}The Oeselians (inhabitants of Saaremaa Island in present-day Estonia) were a powerful seafaring and raiding Baltic-Finnic tribe of the 13th century. Famous for their ships and piracy across the Baltic Sea, they combined farming and fishing with a fierce warrior culture and pagan religious practices. They were among the last northern tribes to resist Christianization, defending their strongholds and sacred groves against crusaders." />
