    <string id="str_culture_description.ushkuiniki_raiders" text="{=ushkuiniki_raidersdescription}The Ushkuiniki were Novgorodian freebooters and raiders who used shallow-draft riverboats called ushkuis. Active from the 12th to 15th centuries, they raided along the Volga, Kama, and into the White Sea, mixing piracy with trade. They represented the adventurous and warlike element of Novgorodian Rus society, combining Slavic traditions, Orthodox faith, and a semi-outlaw lifestyle." />
