    <string id="str_culture_description.mongol_raiders" text="{=mongol_raidersdescription}The Mongols of the 13th century were nomadic steppe warriors who forged one of the largest empires in history. Living in yurts and moving with their herds, they combined exceptional horsemanship and archery with a strict clan hierarchy. Known for their swift raids and disciplined armies, they followed Tengriist traditions alongside shamanic rituals, with authority centered on khans and tribal leaders." />
